{"seq":11,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-sonnet-none-mu-v02-heldout/ms-08-saltmarsh-summary/r3","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T05:38:31.451Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"e5cc61c149651611bafe2536edb16330e553dda202754dfa51f6875316b16743","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Sofia, here are the three answers for the Saltmarsh Provisions handover file.\n\n1. **New owner:** Bettina Kroll took the account over from you on Monday, 6 October 2025. Moss's Coastal digest of 5 Oct 2025 says Saltmarsh \"changes hands tomorrow, Monday, October 6\". It doesn't name the new owner. Bettina is the one the channel and later notes treat as owner. She calls it \"Sofia's old grocery account\" on 17 Nov, and you call it \"Bettina's grocery account\" on 15 Oct. Moss's 18 May 2026 coverage note says the same. The 3 Nov 2025 handoff and the Kwame takeover on 22 Nov are for Pellucid Harbor Logistics, a different account, so leave them out of this summary.\n\n2. **Discount:** 10%. Bettina posted \"12% now\" on 17 Nov 2025 at 14:19. At 14:24 she corrected it: \"please ignore my earlier note, it's 10%\", because she had misread June's draft worksheet. I'm only repeating the figure already posted here. I haven't checked it against the contract or a signed document.\n\n3. **Corinne's admin access ticket:** PD-4827. Kwame opened it on 15 Oct 2025 after Corinne's Pemberline Dock account lost its admin rights. Don't confuse it with PD-4824. That one is a separate ticket about door 3→4 moves showing up in the exception report."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
